  "id": "COMPOUND:39425 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol C appears to have a consistent and significant relationship with H9, as evidenced by three distinct paths that all point to H9 as a target. The first two paths indicate that Certonardosterol C targets Melanocyte protein PMEL, which is then targeted by Idesin and Regaloside C, respectively. The third path provides a more complex pathway, where Certonardosterol C directly targets a metabolite of [(1R,4E,6R,7R,17R)-4-ethylidene-6,7-dimethyl-3,8-dioxo-2,9-dioxa-14-azatricyclo[9.5.1.014,17]heptadec-11-en-7-yl] acetate, which in turn targets H9. All three pathways share a common intermediate, Melanocyte protein PMEL, and the final target, H9, is consistently identified across the evidence.\n\nThe mechanism of action appears to involve the inhibition of a melanocyte protein, which is then targeted by a series of compounds, including Certonardosterol C. This suggests a potential role in modulating melanocyte activity, possibly through the regulation of PMEL or its downstream targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Certonardosterol C and H9, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways and the involvement of different compounds targeting the same intermediate indicate a possible biological relevance, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the therapeutic potential.",
